<title>JAPAN: Kumagai Gumi to dissolve U.S. real estate unit.</title>
<headline>Kumagai Gumi to dissolve U.S. real estate unit.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kumagai Gumi Co Ltd said on Friday that it expects an extraordinary loss of nine billion yen in the year ending on March 31, due to the dissolution of its real estate development subsidiary in the United States.</p>
<p>But the major Japanese construction company said that the loss would be fully offset by sales of a portion of its real estate holdings and securities.</p>
<p>The company said it had decided to dissolve Delaware-based subsidiary Shoreline Holding Corp as it found a bidder for an office building developed by the subsidiary in Corpus Christi, Texas.</p>
</text>
